    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "(a) Estimate $318\\div8$ using $320$.\n(b) Estimate $4741\\div6$ using $4800$. Should the answer be near $80$, $800$ or $8000$?",
        "solution_text": "(a) $320$ is close to $318$ and divides exactly by $8$.\n$318\\div8\\approx320\\div8=40$.\n(b) $4741\\div6\\approx4800\\div6=800$.\nThe answer should be near $800$, not $80$ or $8000$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "For $1885\\div7$, use the nearby multiples $1820$ and $1890$.\n(a) Find lower and upper estimates.\n(b) Which estimate is closer?",
        "solution_text": "(a) $1820\\div7=260$ and $1890\\div7=270$.\nSince $1820<1885<1890$, the quotient is between $260$ and $270$.\n(b) $1885-1820=65$; $1890-1885=5$.\n$1890$ is closer, so $270$ is the closer estimate."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "An estimate for division by $8$ is $420$. Find the compatible number used, then use it to estimate $3327\\div8$.",
        "solution_text": "Compatible number $=8\\times420=3360$.\n$3327\\div8\\approx3360\\div8=420$.\nThis is an upper estimate because $3360>3327$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "(a) Use a lower compatible number to estimate $563\\div9$.\n(b) Use an upper compatible number to estimate $718\\div8$.\n(c) Which of $620$, $630$ and $700$ is the best compatible number for estimating $638\\div7$? Use it to estimate the quotient.",
        "solution_text": "(a) Choose $540$: it is below $563$ and $9\\times60=540$.\n$563\\div9\\approx540\\div9=60$.\n\n(b) Choose $720$: it is above $718$ and $8\\times90=720$.\n$718\\div8\\approx720\\div8=90$.\n\n(c) $620$ does not divide exactly by $7$. Both $630$ and $700$ do, but $630$ is only $8$ from $638$, while $700$ is $62$ away.\n$638\\div7\\approx630\\div7=90$."
      }
    ],
